# PocketBase deployment configuration (Phase 9, #130).
#
# Local dev (`make pb-dev`) reads these from the shell — see the root
# .env.example § "PocketBase migration (#121)" and pocketbase/AUTH.md. This
# file lists the same variables plus the ones only the container needs
# (LITESTREAM_*), for the docker run command in DEPLOYMENT.md. There is no
# .env loader here: dev.sh and the container both take environment variables
# directly, not a file.
#
# --- Names shared with the Django app (config/settings.py) ---
# Same variables, same meaning, so a host already running the Django
# container needs no new secrets when this image replaces it at the Phase 10
# cutover (#131) — see pocketbase/README.md § "Authentication".

# Google OAuth — console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# Redirect URI to register: {origin}/api/oauth2-redirect
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# Microsoft Entra ID — entra.microsoft.com → App registrations
# Redirect URI to register: {origin}/api/oauth2-redirect
# Audience: "Accounts in any organizational directory and personal Microsoft
# accounts" (required for the default `common` tenant).
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=""
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# Comma-separated email addresses granted users.role = ADMIN on OAuth sign-in.
# Empty is a deliberate no-op (leaves existing roles alone), not "demote
# everyone" — see pocketbase/internal/authenv.
ADMIN_EMAILS=""

# Opt into email+password login for accounts that already exist. Self-service
# signup stays OAuth2-only either way (pocketbase/AUTH.md § "The
# password-login decision"). Django's equivalent: DJANGO_ALLOW_PASSWORD_LOGIN.
# GOLFTRACK_ALLOW_PASSWORD_LOGIN="false"

# --- No Django equivalent ---
# Django's DJANGO_SECRET_KEY, DJANGO_ALLOWED_HOSTS and
# DJANGO_CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS have nothing to map here: PocketBase keeps its
# own encryption key in the data directory rather than an env-supplied
# secret, does not validate the request Host header, and issues no
# cookie-based session for a CSRF token to protect — every write is a JSON
# API call carrying an Authorization header (pocketbase/README.md §
# "Frontend"). DATABASE_URL likewise has no equivalent: the data directory
# passed via `--dir` (hardcoded to /data in entrypoint.sh) plays that role.

# Skip the embedded pb_schema.json sync at startup, e.g. while experimenting
# with collections directly in the Admin UI. Leave unset in every deployed
# environment — the sync is what makes the container self-initializing.
# GOLFTRACK_SCHEMA_SYNC="0"

# --- Litestream (S3-compatible replication; see DEPLOYMENT.md) ---
# Unset LITESTREAM_BUCKET makes entrypoint.sh skip replication entirely —
# safe for local `docker run` testing.
LITESTREAM_BUCKET=""
# Region root only, e.g. https://nyc3.digitaloceanspaces.com — do not include
# the bucket name in the hostname (see DEPLOYMENT.md § "Endpoint format
# gotcha").
LITESTREAM_ENDPOINT=""
LITESTREAM_ACCESS_KEY_ID=""
LITESTREAM_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=""
